 See also [`max_width`](#max_width) and [`use_small_heuristics`](#use_small_heuristics)
 
+## `assignment_rhs_break`
+
+Where to break the right-hand side of an assignment, a `let` statement, a `const` or a `static`,
+and the type of a struct field, a type alias or a foreign `static`, that does not fit on the line
+of its left-hand side.
+
+- **Default value**: `"Heuristic"`
+- **Possible values**: `"Heuristic"`, `"TrailingDelimiter"`, `"SameLine"`
+- **Stable**: Yes
+
+#### `"Heuristic"` (default):
+
+The right-hand side moves to the next line when it fits there on one line.
+
+```rust
+fn main() {
+    {
+        {
+            let embodiment =
+                Embodiment::try_from((content, character, session, current_instant, rest))?;
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+#### `"TrailingDelimiter"`:
+
+A right-hand side that ends in a call, a tuple, a struct literal, an array or a macro call, and a
+type that ends in generic arguments, a tuple, a slice or the parameters of a function pointer,
+stays on the line of the left-hand side and breaks inside its trailing delimiter.
+
+```rust
+fn main() {
+    {
+        {
+            let embodiment = Embodiment::try_from((
+                content,
+                character,
+                session,
+                current_instant,
+                rest,
+            ))?;
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+#### `"SameLine"`:
+
+Every right-hand side starts on the line of its `=`, `=>` or `:`: the right-hand side of a `let`,
+an assignment, a `const` or a `static`, the type of a struct field or a type alias, the bounds of a
+where clause or of a trait, the value of a field of a struct literal or a struct pattern, and the
+body of a match arm, whose block opens on that line even behind a guard of several lines. It
+breaks only inside itself, before a binary operator, inside a delimiter, at a link of a chain or
+in the block of a match arm, and where it cannot break at all, such as a long string literal, the
+line grows past `max_width`.
+
+```rust
+fn main() {
+    {
+        {
+            let maybe_moment_milliseconds = playback_milliseconds
+                .checked_rem(duration_milliseconds_value);
+            let expectation = "detail level 1 is 4 by 4 pixels, but half of the level before it is 2 by 2";
+            match vacancy_value {
+                Some(last_vacancy)
+                    if last_vacancy.compose_end_element()
+                        == vacancy.first_element_of_the_page() => {
+                    page_index = last_vacancy.page_index();
+                }
+                _ => {}
+            }
+        }
+    }
+}
+```
+
